  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "185a7a55",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## iTrace dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "94805a3c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This dataset is the output of the iTrace simulation (Community Land Model from iCESM).\n",
    "\n",
    "We download the files at this [link](https://gdex.ucar.edu/datasets/d651022/dataaccess/#), with the naming conventions explained [here](https://yefee.github.io/iTRACE/).\n",
    "\n",
    "The quantity $\\delta^{18}\\text{O}$ is not directly available, we must compute it from the total water trace (H2OTR, in m/s) data and the heavy oxygen water precipitation data (H218O, in m/s).\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    ">The name of the files is consituted of (from left to right)\n",
    "   >\n",
    "   > 1. `b.e13.Bi1850C5`: the machine used for the iTrace simulation\n",
    "   >\n",
    "   > 1. `f19_g16`: the spatial resolution of the simulation (about 1.9° lat x 2.5° lon).\n",
    "   >\n",
    "   > 1. `xxka`: the temporal slice of the simulation (see the documentation for precise info)\n",
    "   >\n",
    "   > 1. `ice_ghg_orb_wtr.0x` or any subset of it : the forcings applied during the simulation.\n",
    "   >\n",
    "   > 1. `clm2`: the Community Land Model version 2 (cam2 for atmoshperic model...)\n",
    "   >\n",
    "   > 1. the name after all is the variable name."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "acea49a0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##### Detailed procedure of the delta 18O computation from itrace files (now wrapped in a more sophisticated function, including snowfall...)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bd282c89",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fn_itrace_H218O = '/media/luluxette/T7 Shield/pdm/iTrace/b.e13.Bi1850C5.f19_g16.12ka.itrace.ice_ghg_orb_wtr.05.clm2.h0.RAIN_H218O.800001-899912.nc'\n",
    "fn_itrace_H2OTR = '/media/luluxette/T7 Shield/pdm/iTrace/b.e13.Bi1850C5.f19_g16.12ka.itrace.ice_ghg_orb_wtr.05.clm2.h0.RAIN_H2OTR.800001-899912.nc'\n",
    "\n",
    "file_H218O = utils.load_xarray_datarray(fn_itrace_H218O)\n",
    "file_H2OTR = utils.load_xarray_datarray(fn_itrace_H2OTR)\n",
    "\n",
    "# print(file_H218O.info())\n",
    "# print(file_H2OTR.info())\n",
    "\n",
    "h218o = file_H218O.RAIN_H218O\n",
    "h2o = file_H2OTR.RAIN_H2OTR"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "f47f0526",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "This dataset covers  1000.0  years at monthly resolution.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print('This dataset covers ',len(h218o.time)/12, ' years at monthly resolution.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "061f9d6b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The fluxes (in mm/s) are actually already corrected for the molar mass and VSMOW standard by the iCESM model (see this [forum](https://bb.cgd.ucar.edu/cesm/threads/how-can-i-use-the-output-variables-of-icesm-to-generate-%CE%B418o-in-atmospheric-precipitation.10990/)). \n",
    "\n",
    "Hence, $R_{^{18}O} = \\frac{n_{^{18}O}}{n_{^{16}O}} = \\frac{f_{^{16}O}}{f_{^{18}O}} $"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "814bd606",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ---- No need of this correction --- \n",
    "# Divide the mm/s by the molar mass to get molar-mass corrected fluxes\n",
    "# M16 = 18.01056468403e-3  # kg/mol\n",
    "# M18 = 20.01481106446e-3\n",
    "# R_vsmow = 0.0020052\n",
    "# mol_ratio = (h218o / h2o) * (M16 / M18)\n",
    "# delta18 = ( mol_ratio / R_vsmow - 1.0) * 1000.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute delta 18 O (per thousand)\n",
    "delta18 = ( h218o/h2o - 1.0) * 1000.0\n",
    "delta18 = delta18.where((h2o > 1e-12)&(delta18 < 100))  # avoid div by near-0 precip values and positive outliers (delta18 should be mostly negative and small -20/+20)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0624679c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The time dimension is defined in days after a random date, we want to chenge this to something more meaningful. According to the [table](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/10WhscwRmVM3FJIPymjcbT6aGKRisAkQ-dnpmxr7Psso/edit?gid=0#gid=0)  linked in [documentation](https://yefee.github.io/iTRACE/), each itrace file contains exactly 1000 years of data at monthly resolution. Thus, we will simply set the time as a number between 1 and 12000, indicating the number of months after the last month of 12kyrBP. Hence, time=1 will refer to the first month of 11999yrBP, etc."
   ]
  },
