   "source": [
    "## RCWIP data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "028e7bde",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "RCWIP2 is a high resolution isoscape (30 arcseconds in all directions) covering all land areas on Earth, for the time period 1960-2016 (no time series, just the mean over this time range). It used model and GNIP data. \n",
    "\n",
    "> The dataset files are in geotif format, by region. Each region is defined as a rectangle covering 30 degrees of latitude and 30 degrees of longitude. Hence, we need some preprocessing to screen the data at itrace resolution and obtain one global dataframe for this dataset. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f67029bb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "loading itrace files\n",
      "This dataset contains  12000  time steps.\n",
      "   bins of width=12000 months (1000 years)\n",
      "   converting xr to DataFrame (~2 minutes)\n",
      "done\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import rasterio \n",
    "from rasterio.transform import xy\n",
    "\n",
    "itrace_df = gutils.get_preprocessed_itrace_data(data_folder="/media/luluxette/T7_Shield/pdm/iTrace/",res=12*1000,format='df',P=False)\n",
    "itrace_df['lon_negpos'] = utils.convert_lon_0_360_to_neg180_180(itrace_df['lon'].values) # type: ignore\n",
    "itrace_locs = itrace_df[['lat','lon','lon_negpos']].drop_duplicates() # type:ignore"
   ]
